      "proof_nodes": [
        {
          "id": "P1",
          "text": "For each finite exponent q>=1, linear Gaussian projections form a continuous linear Lq-valued map. Prove smoothness of the nth power simultaneously in every finite q, using continuous Holder multiplication L^(2q) times L^(2q) into Lq for the successor."
        },
        {
          "id": "P2",
          "text": "Polynomial addition and scalar multiplication assemble the smooth L2 map. Almost-everywhere representatives establish literal membership and identify this map with the displayed toLp map."
        },
        {
          "id": "P3",
          "text": "Specialize to the real image of the integer Hermite polynomial. The toLp representative theorem gives the almost-everywhere identity; lower C-infinity to C2."
        },
        {
          "id": "P4",
          "text": "Expand the finite L2 inner product bilinearly. The existing exact mixed Gaussian Hermite product identity annihilates unequal degrees and gives j! <w,z>^j on the diagonal. No new orthogonality proof is introduced."
        },
        {
          "id": "P5",
          "text": "Finite addition of constant scalar multiples preserves global C2."
        }
      ],
      "private_helper": {
        "name": "smooth_power_ridge",
        "module": "AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/Probability/GaussianPolynomialRidgeSmooth.lean",
        "public_owner": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.GaussianPolynomialRidgeSmooth.standard_gaussian_polynomial_ridge_L2_smooth",
        "reachable": true,
        "reason": "Directly invoked in the monomial branch. Its simultaneous finite-q induction uses Holder multiplication L^(2q) times L^(2q) into Lq, not L2 times L2 into L2.",
        "credit": "Whole-module implementation coverage only; no separate public theorem credit."
